## Conclusion

The primary diagnosis is substantiated: the scratch-kit construction contract
is incompatible with the accepted implementation. Step 0145 requires a
Domain-layer, two-argument, infallible `KitContext.createInMemory`. The canonical
in-memory factory now lives in Storage and initialization returns serialization
errors as values. Domain cannot call Storage without a reference cycle. Fresh
exclusive ownership removes lock contention; it does not remove serialization
or its error channel.

Classify this as a spec/contract conflict following an accepted implementation
change, with a missing forward reconciliation. It is not evidence of an ASG
execution defect or an agent needing another cheap retry. The worker explicitly
reported its incomplete work; the judge and resolver correctly refused to invent
a new construction contract. Repeating the same instructions will not resolve
the contradiction.

Recommend a Storage extension returning `Result<KitContext, KitError>`, reusing
the existing factory. Reconcile the downstream scratch and scene-construction
rules in the same operator ruling. Do not move JSON machinery into Domain,
duplicate the proxy, discard errors, or introduce a compatibility factory.

