## Alternatives and recurrence

Moving/injecting canonical serialization into a lower layer is possible only
with a substantially wider architecture change; it still needs an honest error
contract. Keeping an infallible facade would require throwing or pretending an
initialization error cannot occur. Neither is preferable to the small Storage
extension and an explicit downstream ruling.

This resembles 0052/0056 in its incompatible obligations, but it is a new concrete
construction conflict. The preventive lesson is to trace future consumers when
an accepted change moves a factory or changes its construction dependencies,
and record the resulting binding contract before those slices run. A cheap
retry is ineffective here. The eventual aggregate postmortem analysis can assess
whether ASG should systematically request that forward-impact check; no unverified
ASG defect or tool patch is asserted by this incident.

